captured
route: POST /tasks/<pod>/<id>/retry
status: 200
tack-sends: yes
note: the route takes no body. Captured against a real step-budget stop (round limit, Phase 87
card L's live proof, 2026-11-03): a build step with AGENT_LOOP_MAX_ITERATIONS=3 stopped at its
round limit (hop.budget == {bound: "rounds", limit: 3, used: 3, source: "default", raise:
"AGENT_LOOP_MAX_ITERATIONS", treeChanged: true}) after writing 3 of 6 requested files; this
retry re-ran the same task and the implementer continued its session, writing the 3 remaining
files before stopping again at the same round limit (a second step_budget, not `done` — the
machine's round ceiling never rises between retries, so this is expected and not itself a
finding). A `409` means the retry was already sent; Tack follows the task either way and never
sends a second one (ADR 0038's own note: a retry cannot raise maxTokens).
command: curl -X POST http://127.0.0.1:<port>/tasks/cardl-time/task-00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/retry (bearer token from docket's --token-file)
docket: docket 0.3.0b1 (API 6), source checkout fa06ce05 (rack-cli develop, carries P59-6/7/8)
env: HOME and DOCKET_HOME (a throwaway folder), PATH; provider "local" over an OpenAI-compatible
endpoint at a loopback port (llama.cpp serving a local Qwen checkpoint) — unlike the other
captures in this directory, this one is a live model run, not a no-model refusal
date: 2026-11-03
redacted: the scratch folder, task ids (as an all-zero uuid)
